Instruction for PostProcess.ex (self-standing version)*

*Note that there is an embedded version of postprocessing binaries 
in /NEMO3D/nemo3d/bin directory. Read /NEMO3D/nemo3d/misc/README_POSTPROCESS.

PostProcess.ex [options]: postprocess outputs of NEMO3D.
   1. calculate Coulomb/exchange energies of electron-hole pairs.
   2. calculate dipole moments of electron-hole pair.
   3. project electron/hole wavefunctions into bulk-band Bloch functions.
   4. more to come .......
   * You can turn on/off these tasks with [options]. (see below) 

How to Creat PostProcess.ex:
	cd ../build
	make postprocess
        PostProcess.ex will be created in postprocess/bin directory.

Required files to run PostProcess.ex: 
   -- output files from NEMO3D: 
      	filename.nd_aType (atom type)
      	filename.nd_nbrIndx (nearest neighbor index)
      	filename.nd_rAtom (atom position)
	filename.nd_Ek (electron and hole energy)
 	filename.nd_evec_# (electron and hole wavefunction)
   -- table files for PostProcess:
	coulomb.table (table for coulomb and exchange calculation)
	dipole.table  (table for dipole moment calculation)
        Note:( They are located in ./table directory. 
               Please move them to a directory where you run a code. )
Options to run PostProcess.ex:
   --data filename : specify the filenames of NEMO3D output.
                    (filename.nd_aType, filename.nd_nbrIndx,
                     filename.nd_rAtom, filename.nd_Ek,
                     filename.nd_evec_#)
   --electron n1 n2 n3 ....: 
          n1 is the number of electron wavefunctions to include in calculations.
          n2, n3, ... are the indices of electron wavefunctions to read 
          from filename.nd_evec_n2, filename.nd_evec_n3, ....
          There should be n1 indices of electron wavefunctions.           
   --hole n1 n2 n3 ....:
          n1 is the number of hole wavefunctions to include in calculations.
          n2, n3, ... are the indices of hole wavefunctions to read 
          from filename.nd_evec_n2, filename.nd_evec_n3, ....
          There should be n1 indices of hole wavefunctions.
   --coulomb:
          Coulomb/exchange energies of electron-hole pairs will be calculated.
   --dipole:
          Dipole moments/Oscillator strengths of electron-hole pairs will be calculated.
   --projection:
          Electron/hole wavefunctions will be projected onto bulk-band Bloch functions. 

Example:
   PostProcess.ex --data box --electron 2 6 7 --hole 3 1 2 3 --coulomb --dipole --projection
   What this will do:
   1. box.nd_aType, box.nd_nbrIndx, box.nd_rAtom, box.nd_Ek will be read. 
   2. Two electron wavefunctions will be given by box.nd_evec_6 and box.nd_evec_7.  
   3. Three hole wavefunctions will be given by box.nd_evec_1, box.nd_evec_2, 
      and box.nd_evec_3  
   4. The Coulomb, exchange, dipole moments between the two electron 
      and the three hole wavefunctions will be calculated. 
   5. The two electron wavefunctions and the three hole wavefunctions 
      will be projected into bulk-band Bloch functions.

